    LLM: 'Game: 52 Pick-up. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '52 Pick-up is a social prank using a standard pack: one player offers a game, scatters the cards, and the other player is left to pick them up. It is recorded as a social card-game joke rather than a strategic contest.',
    objective: 'For the target, the only task is to collect the scattered deck and reassemble the pack.',
    gameplay: 'A player asks another person whether they want to play 52 Pick-up. If the invitation is accepted, the first player scatters the 52 cards and announces “52 pick up”. The second person then gathers the cards and restores the deck. There are no turns, scoring, hidden information, or winning strategy beyond recognizing the prank.',
    keyRules: [
      'Requires exactly a normal pack of cards.',
      'The offer to play is part of the joke; scattering the pack creates the task.',
      'No score, winner, or strategic card play is defined.',
    ],
